# cella.policy — the world domains this task is granted.
# <release|refuse> <incoming|outgoing> <destination> (key=value)*
#
# Under the terminated pair (allow_internet=true), titanium routes these
# host grants to the appliance's world-leg border, judged by the name
# the terminator resolves and stamps on each crossing (never a rotating
# ip). The member border (the wire to the appliance) is titanium's own
# fixed grant; only the world names belong here. Everything not granted
# is refused, on the record.
release outgoing example.com:443/tcp (keep_open=5m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming example.com:443/tcp (keep_open=5m)
